    "backend_171": {
        "statement": "",
        "image": [],
        "question": [
            "Give me a description for the following OpenROAD \u2018Placement\u2019 tool variable, GPL_TIMING_DRIVEN?"
        ],
        "question_type": [
            "open"
        ],
        "answer": [
            "In OpenROAD Flow Scripts (ORFS), the GPL_TIMING_DRIVEN variable specifies whether the global placer (gpl) should use timing driven-placement. Timing-driven placement will cause gpl to ocassionally run static timing analysis (sta) during placement in order to determine the timing on each net. gpl will then reweight the nets based on how timing-critical they are. This process improves the timing of the netlist by decreasing the distance between timing-critical cells, but it also causes an increase in gpl runtime due to running timing analysis."
        ],
        "explanation": [
            ""
        ],
        "modality": [
            "text"
        ],
        "difficulty": [
            "medium"
        ],
        "ability": [
            "knowledge"
        ],
        "source": "EDA-Corpus",
        "extra": "Augmented_Data/Question-Answer/Flow/Flow.csv--line-171"
    },
